From b12f65bdb9687d1c8d37d55fe62241959852c033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:02:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Wire dimension 6 (ZIP/county geographic equity) into
 c2_rollup

Closes the other half of the small-gaps list: dimension 6 was built (July
30) but deliberately left unwired, same staged posture dimension 5 had
between being built and being wired in. Same pattern exactly:
CFPBRegBLens.c2_rollup() gains geographic_outcome_equity_findings,
Optional[List[RegulatoryFinding]] = None -- defaults to 'not yet
evaluated' (forces INDETERMINATE), a caller with a real cohort result
passes it through for real. RegulatoryDeck's cohort-equity escalation
(previous commit) now fetches and passes dimension_6_findings alongside
4 and 5, so a mortgage decision in a cohort with a flagged geographic
disparity escalates the same way a demographic one does -- no new
deck-level code needed, the wiring built last commit was already generic
across whichever dimensions c2_rollup accepts.

Every existing c2_rollup call site that asserted PASS or FLAG needed
geographic_outcome_equity_findings=[] added (7 call sites across
test_regulatory_cassettes.py and test_c2_statistical_outcome_equity.py)
-- same requirement dimension 5's wiring imposed on dimension 4's
callers, not a new pattern. Also fixed two docstring references that
still said 'four C2 dimensions' / 'dimension 4 unbuilt' (the second one
pre-dates this session).

New rollup-wiring test section in test_c2_geographic_outcome_equity.py
(6 tests, mirroring dimension 4's proof pattern) -- including a corrected
'reaches PASS' test after the first draft's cohort (ZIP data only) turned
out to always produce a non-empty county-tier indeterminate finding,
never a true empty-findings pass; fixed by populating both tiers.

Full suite 694 passed / 6 skipped, twice back-to-back (required a
ledger_entries reset first -- regulatory_deck.py and cfpb_reg_b.py are
both in the governance code-hash surface, so already-bound test fixtures
in the persistent local Postgres refused under the new hash; documented
pre-existing gotcha, not a regression). Ruff and bandit clean.
